# Optional connection config for `test.sh` — copy to `.env` to point the test at ANY Elasticsearch with
# one value, without passing a variant folder or a URL each time.
#   cp .env.example .env        # then uncomment ONE option below
# `.env` is gitignored. test.sh uses this only when you DON'T pass a TARGET arg or ES_URL.
# (Priority: a URL arg / ES_URL > THIS .env > a per-variant .env > parts/defaults http 127.0.0.1:9200.)
# The test creates + deletes its own throwaway index; the user needs index create/delete rights
# (the variants' built-in `elastic` superuser suffices).

# Option A — a single base URL (with credentials):
# ES_URL=http://elastic:yourpassword@127.0.0.1:9200

# Option B — individual parts:
# ES_SCHEME=http
# ES_HOST=127.0.0.1
# ES_HTTP_PORT=9200
# ES_USER=elastic
# ELASTIC_PASSWORD=yourpassword
